---
title: Spiced Roasted Cauliflower with Tahini Sauce
author: Jonathan Simmonds
servings: 6
cook time: 40 minutes
---

Toss @cauliflower{2%large}(cut into florets) with @extra virgin olive oil{5%tbsp} and @cumin{4%tsp}, @smoked paprika{2%tsp}, @turmeric{2%tsp}, @cayenne{2%tsp} or @hot chilli powder{1%tsp}, and @garlic powder{4%tsp}.

Roast at 200°C for ~{40%minutes}, turning every ~{10%minutes} until crisp and golden. 10 minutes before they are done, add @pine nuts{50%g}(toasted).

Mix @tahini{125%g}, @lemon{1}(juiced), @honey{2%tbsp}, and @garlic{2%cloves}(crushed) to make the sauce and whisk to combine. Add warm @water{} a little bit at a time, and continue whisking, until it reaches the desired consistency. Add @salt{} and @black pepper{} to taste.

Drizzle the sauce over the cauliflower. Set some aside for the table.

> This dish is great for gatherings and pairs well with fresh parsley.

> Pairs well with @./sides/lentil-bulgar-pilaf{1}.
